Maniac wrote:
> Some of the topics that Rast asked to have updated include:
>  o recommending a ring of conflict in the mid to end game period

Yes, definitely.  Not only do monsters attack each other, but in doing
so they attack you less.  Which is equivalent to free AC and HP.  The
penalty for it on Astral is a complete joke compared to the benefits.

>  o several possible changes for wishing to include:
>   - what to wish for if you get an early chance

Not that it's particularly insightful, but blessed +3 GDSM or an
MR-granting artifact should be at the top of this list (if you lack
MR).

>   - recommending +3 instead of +2 for SOME of the items

Almost always. The expect value for wishing for +3 is +1.8 on average.
The expected value for +2 is +1.6 on average.  Long-term you're better
off wishing for +3 all the time.  Short term, even +2 is only 4/5 of
the time, +3 is 3/5 of the time; it really isn't as though the +2 is a
lock.
I _will_ wish for 2 scrolls or potions if the incremental value of a
third one isn't worth the chance of losing the 2nd.  But for
weapon/armor enchantments I personally never feel it's worth the
tradeoff unless there's a very odd reason other than the standard
hit/damage/AC of the enchantment (helm of brilliance would be the only
think I'd consider wishing +2, but even then I'd probably feel +3 is a
wiser choice).

>   - NOT recommending gauntlets of dexterity nor of power

They're pretty wasteful wishes.  If I had tons of early luck and so had
the rest of my armor/weapons/some markers/etc then I _might_ consider
the GoP for a character who's an inept spellcaster and has a low Str,
but that's a very low priority and it's for an item that I'd probably
be abandoning soon enough anyway.

>   - should we recommend dip into fountains (or not) to get a wish

It is a good idea for characters for whom a wish is a big deal (e.g.
lacking MR or reflection) and who can easily deal with water demons,
nymphs, and water moccasins (obviously stashing your gold out of pool
of water range first).  Water moccasins can summon tougher demons, so
you have to consider the odds of that (and how dangerous it is) vs. the
danger of not having MR/reflection and the odds of getting the wish.

It is also worth recommending that once you reach a point where dipping
for excalibur is a good play, it's probably worth starting with the
highest fountains in the dungeon--if you're incurring the dipping
risks, you may as well maximize the wish odds while you're at it.
However, if a wish is very high priority and you're planning to dip for
it, this may not be the case--you could get excalibur and eliminate a
higher-percentage wish fountain in the process.
If you're dipping to remove a curse, then starting at the highest level
fountains is a clear win.

Also perhaps worth explaining what a Castle dive is and when it makes
sense (not the full-out early reckless "Dive for Victory", but the
controlled dive for a character who's explored everything above DL8 and
is reasonably tough and yet lacks crucial items, where proceeding to
the Castle with all deliberate haste may be the best percentage play).



